# Test: a monitor line with a chain over SSH exec is rendered by the daemon and accounted as typed
#
# The one question: when an SSH client sends a monitor line with a chain on
# the exec channel and sets no rendering key, does the daemon apply the whole
# chain to the stream (only the lines `| match state` keeps arrive), and does
# the TACACS+ accounting START record hold the line as typed, chain included?
# TestExecStreamPassesTypedLine and TestSSHExecStreamAccountsAndAuthorizesTyped
# Line prove the pieces in process; only a daemon proves the exec channel, the
# stream route, the event monitor and the TACACS+ client agree on one line.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-pipe-chain-honored-on-every-command-surface AC-22 and AC-35
#   (SSH exec), user story 7.
# PREVENTS: the stream route accounting and authorizing the command part
#   alone (`ProcessRemoteStreamPipes` splits the chain off before the stream
#   factory runs, internal/component/ssh/ssh.go execMiddleware), so a policy
#   or an audit reads a line nobody typed.
#
# Red at 5ebf3c1c8e (run 2026-11-20 19:19): the accounting record held the
#   typed line, and the stream ended on the first OPEN event with "match
#   needs rows, and this answer has none: it holds one document": every
#   stream ran its chain over each event as if it were a one-shot answer, so
#   `| match` refused an event that is one document. A stream's rows are its
#   events: applyEventMatch (internal/component/command/pipe.go) keeps or
#   removes such an event whole, TestStreamLineMatchKeepsWholeEvents.
#
# The mock writes its own stderr, so its quotes print plain (records.go).
#
# The barrier: StreamEventMonitor subscribes, then writes its header
# ("monitoring: include=open,state"), which `match state` keeps, so the
# driver brings the BGP session up only after the subscription exists. The
# OPEN events ({"type":"bgp",...,"message":{"type":"open",...}}) hold no
# "state" and are dropped; the state event ({"type":"state",...,"state":"up"})
# is kept. A line holding "open" in quotes proves the chain was not applied.
#
# Method: internal/test/fixture ssh_exec_line.go (plugin/ssh-exec-line): an
# x/crypto/ssh client logs in as admin (TACACS+ mock, PAP), sends the line on
# an exec channel, waits for the header, completes a dynamic BGP handshake
# as AS65001 on $PORT3 (monitor_remote_as_stream.go's session), and returns
# once a line holding "up" arrived, which ends the monitor.

option=timeout:value=60s

tmpfs=monitor.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
system {
	authentication {
		tacacs {
			server 127.0.0.1 { port $PORT; key "ze-mock-key"; }
			timeout 2
			authorization true
			accounting true
		}
		tacacs-profile 15 { profile [ admin ]; }
	}
	authorization {
		profile admin { run { default-action allow; } edit { default-action allow; } }
	}
}
environment {
	ssh {
		enabled true
		server main {
			ip 127.0.0.1;
			port $PORT2;
		}
	}
}
bgp {
	group dynamic-monitor {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip dynamic
				connect false
				range 127.0.0.1/32
			}
			local {
				ip 127.0.0.1
				port $PORT3
				accept true
			}
		}
		session {
			asn { local 65000; }
			router-id 1.1.1.1
			family {
				ipv4/unicast { prefix { maximum 10000; } }
			}
			capability { graceful-restart disable; }
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=le mock tacacs --port $PORT --key ze-mock-key --user admin:testpass:15:name=tacacs:ready=le mock tacacs: listening on
expect=stderr:pattern=ACCT START seq=[0-9]+ total=[0-9]+ cmd="monitor event include open,state \| match state"
reject=stderr:pattern=ACCT START .*cmd="monitor event include open,state"

cmd=background:seq=2:exec=ze start monitor.conf:name=daemon:ready=Ze running.

cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=le test fixture plugin/ssh-exec-line stream $PORT2 $PORT3 'monitor event include open,state | match state' up open:timeout=45s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=OK: monitor event include open,state | match state printed up and no line holding open
reject=stderr:contains=ZE-OBSERVER-FAIL

cmd=stop:seq=4:name=daemon:signal=term
cmd=stop:seq=5:name=tacacs:signal=term
